  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LPI Ethiopia Programme 2023 to 2026 - Sowing the Seeds of Peace in Ethiopia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">LPI Ethiopia Programme 2023 to 2026 - Sowing the Seeds of Peace in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Life &amp; Peace Institute (LPI) har varit en l&#xe5;ngvarig partner till Sverige i dess globala, regionala och olika bilaterala strategier. LPI Addis Abeba Office &#xf6;vervakar b&#xe5;de f&#xf6;r Afrikas horn-programmet (HARP) och Etiopien-programmet. 

LPI har st&#xf6;tt lokalt drivna fredsbyggande initiativ i Etiopien sedan 1991 genom partnerskap med samh&#xe4;llen inklusive traditionella ledare och civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer. Denna intervention ses som den andra fasen av LPI Etiopienprogram som st&#xf6;ddes av Sverige genom sin bilaterala strategi fr&#xe5;n 2017 till 2022. 

Syftet med denna intervention &#xe4;r att v&#xe5;rda och uppr&#xe4;tth&#xe5;lla civilsamh&#xe4;llesledda, inkluderande fredsbyggande processer f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rebyggande, hantering och l&#xf6;sning av konflikter med fredliga medel i Etiopien. 

Den totala budgeten som f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra LPI Etiopienprogram under fyra &#xe5;r (2023 &#x2013; 2026) &#xe4;r 75,7 MSEK och Sveriges bidrag kommer att vara totalt 44 MSEK under fyra &#xe5;r med start april 2023.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Life &amp; Peace Institute (LPI) has been a long-time partner to Sweden in its Global, regional and various bilateral strategies. LPI Addis Ababa Office oversees both for the Horn of Africa Programme (HARP) and the Ethiopia Programme. 

LPI has supported locally driven peace building initiatives in Ethiopia since 1991 through partnerships with communities including traditional leaders and civil society organisations. This intervention is seen as the second phase of LPI&#x2019;s Ethiopia Programme that was supported by Sweden through its bilateral strategy from 2017 until 2022. 

The objective of this intervention is to nurture and sustain civil society-led, inclusive peace building processes for prevention, management and resolution of conflicts by peaceful means in Ethiopia. 

The total budget expected for implementing the LPI&#x2019;s Ethiopia Programme over four years (2023 &#x2013; 2026) is 75.7 MSEK and Sweden&apos;s contribution will be a total of 44 MSEK for four years starting April 2023.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the programme is:

Nurture and sustain civil society-led, inclusive peacebuilding processes for prevention, management and resolution of conflicts by peaceful means in Ethiopia.

Objective 1: The role of Ethiopian peacebuilding CSOs in dialogue and reconciliation efforts at the national, regional and community levels is enhanced.? 

Objective 2: Stakeholders in and around the universities take collaborative action to promote peaceful and inclusive campuses and communities.? 

Objective 3: Increased collective actions to address causes/drivers of conflict within and between communities sustainably.? 

Objective 4: Relevant policy stakeholders?take actions that support inclusive dialogue and,?reconciliation processes and peace building in Ethiopia.?</narrative>
  </description>
